{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book","id":1496181,"title":"Sphere and rank for locating pieces of a broken book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-11-04T02:52:24-07:00","id":1496181,"title":"Sphere and rank for locating pieces of a broken book","content":"What would be the sphere rank needed for knowing the locations of pages of a book that\u2019s been ripped into pieces and spread around in hundreds of kilometers apart?<br /> <br /> Correspondence and matter or entropy rank 1 with a lot of successes needed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27571-maestrim","name":"Maestrim","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T03:53:25-07:00","id":1496183,"title":"","content":"It really depends on how many mundane steps you're willing to take in this, and how fast you want to do it.<br /> <br /> The real big consideration for how many successes it would take is going to be how you know about it, and what you have as a sympathetic connection to the original book.<br /> <br /> In theory if you have, say, a piece of the original? You can justify Correspondence 2 alone, with minimal successes, but each casting is one success and you either need to go get it yourself or use other magic to retrieve it.<br /> <br /> The less ideal things get, the more legwork to do, or the more powerful magic you'll need to employ.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T04:34:24-07:00","id":1496184,"title":"","content":"Yes, knowing the location is Correspondence 2, you only need Matter if you are pulling them to you. The difficulty is going to be in number of successes or number of castings. A spell to find all of them will need as many successes as there are pieces (1 for the spell and 1 for each additional target), so 6 pages means 6 successes. You can also cast the spell as many times as there are pieces, which is probably the only reasonable option if there are a lot of pages. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T04:41:05-07:00","id":1496185,"title":"","content":"Corr 3/Matter (optional Entropy 1 if you're worried about physically getting to the pages rather than just knowing their location) could do a map of all the pieces and would get around the huge number of successes of doing it once each. Life might be needed if you wanted to phyiscally colocate yourself to each position to grab the pages, and Mind 1 to handle the mental strain.<br /> <br /> It would still be a lot of successes to rack up, even if not as many as one caster per piece could be.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T07:48:04-07:00","id":1496194,"title":"","content":"With a piece of the book, Time 2, Matter 3 and Prime 2 you should be able to rebuild it good as new, too!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T09:37:47-07:00","id":1496201,"title":"","content":"Ultimately the challenge here has more to do with external conditions like where they are, how fast you need to reclaim them, who is watching/guarding them, etc. A lot of things are fairly easy for mages (time consuming or tedious perhaps, but easy) if they have unlimited time. Time limits and complications are the way to add tension to the challenge.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-04T15:42:57-07:00","id":1496227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1496194#post1496194\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With a piece of the book, Time 2, Matter 3 and Prime 2 you should be able to rebuild it good as new, too!</div> </div> </div> </div>I immediately started trying to a solution that would benefit from using Time2. If the storyteller allows for the Time Sight to be maintained with concentration, the success threshold could be bypassed that way. Just remembered from another post, this is a beginning chronicle. None of them are likely to have that combination of spheres.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27571-maestrim\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"27571\" data-vbnamecard=\"27571\">Maestrim</a>, did the person throw the shredded pile from a balcony on a windy day, drive around flicking pieces out the window, employ a group of people to spread them or some other method? This will affect what methods can be used to reassemble or recreate the book, both magical and mundane.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T07:59:39-08:00","id":1496910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1496227#post1496227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I immediately started trying to a solution that would benefit from using Time2. If the storyteller allows for the Time Sight to be maintained with concentration, the success threshold could be bypassed that way. Just remembered from another post, this is a beginning chronicle. None of them are likely to have that combination of spheres.<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span>, did the person throw the shredded pile from a balcony on a windy day, drive around flicking pieces out the window, employ a group of people to spread them or some other method? This will affect what methods can be used to reassemble or recreate the book, both magical and mundane.</div> </div> </div> </div>Time 2 Mind 1 would probably be the easiest solution to simply memorize all the pages down to the tiniest letter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T18:28:49-08:00","id":1496954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1496910#post1496910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Time 2 Mind 1 would probably be the easiest solution to simply memorize all the pages down to the tiniest letter.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, and the retype it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-12T19:54:18-08:00","id":1496955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1496954#post1496954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes, and the retype it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. This will be all that is needed if all that is needed is to replicate the content; only if it is some sort of magical book that requires the original pages to work its mojo is that this wont do - in which case, neither would it be effective to use matter to rebuild the pages either. You would need indeed to physically locate the pages using Correspondence - or, in the most hardcore case in which the pages have been destroyed, you would need some combination of Correspondence 2 with Archsphere Time (Time 6 probably, depending on wether you use level 6 Spheres as the upper limit like I do, or if you use the horrible ideas on &quot;Masters of the Arts&quot; with Archspheres up to 10, which I personally hate), to physically &quot;snatch&quot; them from the past.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-21T11:40:56-08:00","id":1497739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1496955#post1496955\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Exactly. This will be all that is needed if all that is needed is to replicate the content; only if it is some sort of magical book that requires the original pages to work its mojo is that this wont do - in which case, neither would it be effective to use matter to rebuild the pages either. You would need indeed to physically locate the pages using Correspondence (...)</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe also Entropy Magick (or maybe even a Prime Effect) could be used to achieve such outcome / result ? I do recall Entropy divination or perception Effects being mentioned relatively often in some M:tA books. It might require higher Sphere level than Entropy at 1 or 2, at such Effects might be relatively rare among Technocrats and Traditiion Mages, at least going by the usual tendencies and themes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T04:57:25-08:00","id":1497899,"title":"","content":"Time 2, Correspondance 2 would also work. Just grab it before it's destroyed. The only caveat is you need to return it to the time you took it from or there will be paradox and Paradox!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-23T13:13:03-08:00","id":1497939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1497899#post1497899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Time 2, Correspondance 2 would also work. Just grab it before it's destroyed. The only caveat is you need to return it to the time you took it from or there will be paradox and Paradox!</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you need Time 4 for that, because you are reaching into the past.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-24T04:13:19-08:00","id":1497978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1497739#post1497739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe also Entropy Magick (or maybe even a Prime Effect) could be used to achieve such outcome / result ? I do recall Entropy divination or perception Effects being mentioned relatively often in some M:tA books. It might require higher Sphere level than Entropy at 1 or 2, at such Effects might be relatively rare among Technocrats and Traditiion Mages, at least going by the usual tendencies and themes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, if you add Prime 4 you could &quot;repair&quot; the magic part of the book - if it isnt completely ruined. If losing the pages just left the book's mojo &quot;damaged&quot;, adding Prime 4 could &quot;realign&quot; the new pages with its ether fluctuations. No further Spheres needed (no need to add Entropy).<br /> <br /> So, Time 2 and Corr 2 to &quot;get in touch&quot; with the original pages, Matter 2 to physically &quot;copy&quot; the pages, and Prime 4 to &quot;copy the Ether&quot; of the pages, to align their &quot;prime fluctuations&quot; with that of the book. This is the clean requirements to do it, and the easiest way (as opposed to snatching them from the past - or the future).<br /> <br /> In case the pages arent destroyed thou, but cant be snatched (they are protected for example), you could still do this to copy them from the past (before whomever is guarding them now gotta a hold on them), you can copy them, but you'll need to &quot;cut off&quot; the originals' link with the book, in order for the new pages to &quot;suck in&quot; the Ether. Otherwise the magic wont work - this is, after all, a &quot;magic transfer&quot;, you are &quot;sucking up&quot; all of the mojo contained on the originals, and transferring it to a new vessel, therefore the originals will need to get removed. Since this would also be Prime 1, it will only add extra successes required (for something that will already be quite hard to begin with)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HorizonParty2021</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1497939#post1497939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you need Time 4 for that, because you are reaching into the past.</div> </div> </div> </div>Reaching into the <b>future</b> is Time 5.Theoretically, reaching into the <b>past</b> would be Time 6 (or more, if you play with levels above 6 - which I dont).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-24T09:25:43-08:00","id":1497997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1497978#post1497978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, if you add Prime 4 you could &quot;repair&quot; the magic part of the book - if it isnt completely ruined. If losing the pages just left the book's mojo &quot;damaged&quot;, adding Prime 4 could &quot;realign&quot; the new pages with its ether fluctuations. No further Spheres needed (no need to add Entropy).<br /> <br /> So, Time 2 and Corr 2 to &quot;get in touch&quot; with the original pages, Matter 2 to physically &quot;copy&quot; the pages, and Prime 4 to &quot;copy the Ether&quot; of the pages, to align their &quot;prime fluctuations&quot; with that of the book. This is the clean requirements to do it, and the easiest way</div> </div> </div> </div>Could this be a Coincidental Effect under some circumstances?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-25T04:19:58-08:00","id":1498032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1497997#post1497997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could this be a Coincidental Effect under some circumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes it could.<br /> <br /> In your Sanctum or at the Umbra haha.<br /> <br /> Seriously thou, no need to do such an elaborate ritual at the street. Just to come up with it should take a good amount of research.<br /> <br /> And yes, absolutely Vulgar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T03:51:40-08:00","id":1498066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1497997#post1497997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could this be a Coincidental Effect under some circumstances?</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Actually, I know a monastery in Tibet that has a copy&quot;<br /> &quot;With the three pages we have and using advanced heuristic modelling our machine learning algorithms should be able to reproduce the book content within a 97% accuracy interval&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":1182,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","user":"Asmodai","date":". 11-26-2022, 06:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-26T09:15:59-08:00","id":1498085,"title":"","content":"I mean, the simple answer as long as you're not extended beyond sensory range for anything other that perceiving the book fragments: you do it in a properly aligned Sanctum. No need to come up with any sort of contrived situation. Unless it's common knowledge to Sleeper society that only one copy of the book was known to exist, and that it was since destroyed, there's no risk of you taking it out of the Sanctum and problems cropping up like if you give yourself wings and then leave a Sanctum. Any magical attributes of the text that have been reconstructed aren't (probably) inherently vulgar, so that's not a problem either.<br /> <br /> The coincidental/vulgar line is what a hypothetical average observer would consider as they watch you cast the spell. No amount of plausible explanations after the spell is cast justifies it if the book just pops into existence next to you just because no real Sleeper is there to see it; even if you want to have such explanations in handy for later.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T05:23:27-08:00","id":1498205,"title":"","content":"If you aren't worried about matching the original appearance, you can claim eidetic memory abilities that let you just write or type out the book. You might even be able to claim your foci as mnemonic devices that help you recall things. The technological variant of this is even easier: claim you have a digital backup and print it out. Unless there is a physical manifestation of the Prime realignment you probably don't need to worry about explaining that part. <br /> <br /> If you need to match the appearance and physical characteristics of the original book you will probably need to either bring some pre-aged materials or incorporate some Hollywood forging techniques like ironing the pages, spraying them down with coffee, or burying the new book for a few days.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T10:25:40-08:00","id":1498217,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1498066#post1498066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;Actually, I know a monastery in Tibet that has a copy&quot;<br /> &quot;With the three pages we have and using advanced heuristic modelling our machine learning algorithms should be able to reproduce the book content within a 97% accuracy interval&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the second description written in regard to Technocrat Mages, or possibly Tradition Mages from the Society of the Ether? The description definitely seems very tilted towards such or similar groups.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-28T14:14:20-08:00","id":1498230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1498217#post1498217\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the second description written in regard to Technocrat Mages, or possibly Tradition Mages from the Society of the Ether? The description definitely seems very tilted towards such or similar groups.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well yes, it's just a technomantic justification.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T11:25:29-08:00","id":1498461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1498230#post1498230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well yes, it's just a technomantic justification.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to be noted that the vast majority of M:tA is written strictly from the perspective of Tradition Mages - in fact it might be even more narrow, with the average narrator or protagonist of a M:tA book being a Hermetic, a Chakravanti, a Chorister, an Akashic, or a Verbenae. Stories or descriptions written strictly for and in regard to viewpoints of different Mage groups - Mystic Nephandi Mages, the Technepandi, Hollow Ones, Crafts, Technomancers (from the Traditions), or various Technocrats - are rather rare. Though some are of course of excellent quality, as it is Mage: the Ascension and WoD after all.<br /> <br /> Thus I consider it that every mention, analysis and expansion that details groups other than the Traditions is needed and is certainly a positive contribution in M:tA's development. Though of course as a devoted and avid M:tA fan, supporter, and enthusiast I'm all Tradition Mages being prominently and extensively featured and described throughout Mage: the Ascension books and rules systems. Even currently some of the basic and most prominent groups, social clubs, and organizations within invidual Traditions definitely need more details and extensive descriptions and outlines. The Paradigms of various and different Tradition Mages could also be described nicely and perfectly to a more considerable and significant extent. Also more prose, vigenettes, and short stories about Tradition Mages (and other Mages, like Technocrats from the NWO, the Progenitors, and the Syndicate) would be most welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T00:42:15-08:00","id":1499038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1498205#post1498205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you need to match the appearance and physical characteristics of the original book you will probably need to either bring some pre-aged materials or incorporate some Hollywood forging techniques like ironing the pages, spraying them down with coffee, or burying the new book for a few days.</div> </div> </div> </div>...or using Matter 2..<br /> EDIT: and even more successes, depending on how much EXACTLY IDENTICAL the pages need to be... I'd say that if you need the pages to be 100.1% identical to the originals (to the point that they are, in fact, the originals), you would require some 10 extra successes, on top of the successes already required for everything else, so I'd say that this would be a 20 successes ritual, at least for the most hardcore version of it were you literally REMAKES the pages of a magik book down to the tiniest atom and to the tiniest &quot;ethereal wave function&quot;, perfectly preserving (and restoring) all of it's original mojo, to the point where those &quot;new&quot; pages arent exactly new, but rather are the ORIGINAL pages (even if the actual original pages are still out there somewhere). That would be AT LEAST 20 successes (or more)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24689,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","user":"Kakost","date":". 12-07-2022, 03:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T01:22:39-08:00","id":1499040,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1498461#post1498461\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It has to be noted that the vast majority of M:tA is written strictly from the perspective of Tradition Mages - in fact it might be even more narrow, with the average narrator or protagonist of a M:tA book being a Hermetic, a Chakravanti, a Chorister, an Akashic, or a Verbenae. Stories or descriptions written strictly for and in regard to viewpoints of different Mage groups - Mystic Nephandi Mages, the Technepandi, Hollow Ones, Crafts, Technomancers (from the Traditions), or various Technocrats - are rather rare. Though some are of course of excellent quality, as it is Mage: the Ascension and WoD after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would disagree a little bit in here. I'd say that overall, Mage is largely described in Hermetic terms, but also on very heavy Technocratic elements. And that holds true for both the official books and for how the player base communicates. And when other Paradigms are in play, this &quot;Techno-hermetic&quot; language gets &quot;translated&quot; to it.<br /> <br /> The best example is perhaps, how the Sphere of Entropy is understood. Entropy is perhaps the least understood Sphere of all exactly because it is best understood in &quot;technocratic&quot; terms - but Mage is a game where you ALWAYS start as a &quot;Traditional Mage&quot; rather than trying to figure it out from the pov of the Union from the get go.<br /> <br /> So, Entropy is, in a sense, &quot;quantic manipulation&quot;, there is, you make tiny, miniscule changes at a quantum level, that add up to a monumental effect, which the mystics call &quot;destiny&quot; or &quot;fortune&quot;. Even the name itself is from a scientific therm, rather than it being called &quot;Fortuna Sphere&quot;, so right there you already are receiving technocratic jargon. And then, once the concept is understood, it gets &quot;translated&quot; to other paradigms (oh, so it's the manipulation of Fate/Destiny/Chance? Cool).<br /> <br /> There are several other examples thou, and they cut both ways: Spirit and Prime for example are mostly explained in hermetic terms, and once it is understood by the players, the Guide to the Technocracy &quot;translates&quot; them to technocratic verbatim.<br /> <br /> And the reason for this is simple: &quot;technocratic paradigm&quot; is basically our middle school science, mixed with a little bit of techno-babble for style, and &quot;hermetic paradigm&quot; is mostly pop culture mysticism. So that's why those too are the used &quot;codes&quot; for Mage the Ascension, because it is simple and easy to understand, and easy to compile into complex ideas, made digestible enough to be used in a game of RPG, rather than requiring a PhD in Natural Sciences or in Anthropology to play. So, what is Prime? It&quot;s &quot;Meta-Magic&quot;, the Sphere that deals with &quot;magic fluctuations&quot; (know as &quot;Mana&quot; in many games, &quot;Quintessence&quot; in MtA). What is Entropy? Manipulation of chance. So why not just call it &quot;Fortune&quot; or &quot;Destiny&quot;? Because you need to understand a bit of middle school science in order to understand each one of its levels. What is &quot;Spirit&quot;? Manipulation of &quot;ephemeral&quot; entities (commonly know as &quot;spirits&quot;), and so on, so forth.<br /> <br /> Do you wanna see other Spheres with heavy techno-languages in them? Matter, Forces, Life. Forces may even be a better example, since to understand what Forces do, you have to know what is Kinetic Energy, Thermal Energy, Light, Sound and Electromagnetic (oh yes, and Gravity, almost forgot that one). Again, all of that, middle school science.<br /> <br /> For Matter, think about Matter 5... Change *density*... Basically everything Matter 5 does relates to some knowledge we earned in middle school science.<br /> <br /> And then, all of those get &quot;translated&quot; to a mystic paradigm. The player using Matter 5 to create a &quot;Sword of the Heavens&quot; will claim to the Master that he wants to &quot;bless his sword&quot; IN GAME, and OFF GAME he explains to the Master he's using Matter 5 to &quot;increase the density&quot; of the sword.<br /> <br /> A techno-boy explains to the Master that he's using &quot;Spirit (Dimensional Science) 4&quot; to &quot;trap the spirit (alien anomaly)&quot; in the ship's warp drive, and thus explains how he uses his &quot;quantum modulators&quot; to attune the anomaly wave-lenght to that of the drive, thus concluding the procedure.<br /> <br /> See? It's a common techno-hermetic background that gets translated into whatever babble the Mage's paradigm is.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T05:49:53-08:00","id":1499057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1499038#post1499038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...or using Matter 2..<br /> EDIT: and even more successes, depending on how much EXACTLY IDENTICAL the pages need to be... I'd say that if you need the pages to be 100.1% identical to the originals (to the point that they are, in fact, the originals), you would require some 10 extra successes, on top of the successes already required for everything else, so I'd say that this would be a 20 successes ritual, at least for the most hardcore version of it were you literally REMAKES the pages of a magik book down to the tiniest atom and to the tiniest &quot;ethereal wave function&quot;, perfectly preserving (and restoring) all of it's original mojo, to the point where those &quot;new&quot; pages arent exactly new, but rather are the ORIGINAL pages (even if the actual original pages are still out there somewhere). That would be AT LEAST 20 successes (or more)</div> </div> </div> </div>I was just addressing steps you might take to make your spell look coincidental. Hollywood aging techniques are not going remove the Sphere costs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-07T12:16:21-08:00","id":1499090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1499057#post1499057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I was just addressing steps you might take to make your spell look coincidental. Hollywood aging techniques are not going remove the Sphere costs.</div> </div> </div> </div>Got it \ud83d\udc4d<br /> I thought you were suggesting using purely (*cof cof cof*) mundane measures for it (&quot;so uncivilized&quot;).<br /> <br /> I mean, why using mundane means when magick makes everything easier? Right?<br /> <br /> Oh common, dont start talking about &quot;ooh hubris&quot; and stuff to me! Im the humblest guy, and totally in control! Just trust me!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T02:23:56-08:00","id":1499132,"title":"","content":"I think the effect could be done with Corr1 alone, but with Matter 1 would be easier.<br /> <br /> Corr 1 would allow you to sense connections to the book, but can also sense distance and dirrection.<br /> <br /> You should with corr 1 alone be able to feel out all connections to the book and focus on any one of them to determine what direction they are in relation to the book, and how far away they are from the book.<br /> <br /> With corr alone you could only focus on connection strength, so body sample (piece of book) would likely be the strongest, but so too could author of book, or where the book is most regarded. So it would be a bit of a crapshoot to know which connection to focus on.<br /> <br /> Matter 1 would let you filter connections based on matter patterns, so you could focus specifically on matter pattern connections, reducing the guesswork.<br /> <br /> Because corr 2 would be required to see where the pages are, not could you do any alaysis on the pages with other spheres (mattet to see what they are made of, prime to see if they quintessence, etc) without corr 2, it should be emphasised that info from corr 1 is very limited only to of direction and distance from connection, with over spheres simply helping in defining the search.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":12193,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","user":"Saikou","date":". 12-08-2022, 06:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T05:42:17-08:00","id":1499139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1499132#post1499132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the effect could be done with Corr1 alone, but with Matter 1 would be easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, with Corr 1 alone you could locate them pages. The many additional options were for covering any possible scenario (with the examples of the pages having being destroyed and it being a magic book that can only properly work with those missing pages).<br /> <br /> But if all that you want is to locate the detached pages and PHYSICALLY GO TO THEM, indeed Corr 1 alone would suffice.<br /> <br /> But again, in this easiest option, you would have a GPS to them, and would need to walk over to the place they are. If that's feasible to do, ok. Pretty simple, the pages would probably count as &quot;body sample&quot;, so you would only really need enough successes to keep the effect on until you reach them, so probably just enough for it to last for a day, unless it is in another continent or some such.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-08T09:57:58-08:00","id":1499147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kakost</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1496181-sphere-and-rank-for-locating-pieces-of-a-broken-book?p=1499040#post1499040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I would disagree a little bit in here. I'd say that overall, Mage is largely described in Hermetic terms, but also on very heavy Technocratic elements. And that holds true for both the official books and for how the player base communicates. And when other Paradigms are in play, this &quot;Techno-hermetic&quot; language gets &quot;translated&quot; to it.<br /> <br /> The best example is perhaps, how the Sphere of Entropy is understood. Entropy is perhaps the least understood Sphere of all exactly because it is best understood in &quot;technocratic&quot; terms - but Mage is a game where you ALWAYS start as a &quot;Traditional Mage&quot; rather than trying to figure it out from the pov of the Union from the get go.<br /> <br /> So, Entropy is, in a sense, &quot;quantic manipulation&quot;, there is, you make tiny, miniscule changes at a quantum level, that add up to a monumental effect, which the mystics call &quot;destiny&quot; or &quot;fortune&quot;. Even the name itself is from a scientific therm, rather than it being called &quot;Fortuna Sphere&quot;, so right there you already are receiving technocratic jargon. And then, once the concept is understood, it gets &quot;translated&quot; to other paradigms (oh, so it's the manipulation of Fate/Destiny/Chance? Cool).<br /> <br /> There are several other examples thou, and they cut both ways: Spirit and Prime for example are mostly explained in hermetic terms, and once it is understood by the players, the Guide to the Technocracy &quot;translates&quot; them to technocratic verbatim.<br /> <br /> And the reason for this is simple: &quot;technocratic paradigm&quot; is basically our middle school science, mixed with a little bit of techno-babble for style, and &quot;hermetic paradigm&quot; is mostly pop culture mysticism. So that's why those too are the used &quot;codes&quot; for Mage the Ascension, because it is simple and easy to understand, and easy to compile into complex ideas, made digestible enough to be used in a game of RPG, rather than requiring a PhD in Natural Sciences or in Anthropology to play. So, what is Prime? It&quot;s &quot;Meta-Magic&quot;, the Sphere that deals with &quot;magic fluctuations&quot; (know as &quot;Mana&quot; in many games, &quot;Quintessence&quot; in MtA). What is Entropy? Manipulation of chance. So why not just call it &quot;Fortune&quot; or &quot;Destiny&quot;? Because you need to understand a bit of middle school science in order to understand each one of its levels. What is &quot;Spirit&quot;? Manipulation of &quot;ephemeral&quot; entities (commonly know as &quot;spirits&quot;), and so on, so forth.<br /> <br /> Do you wanna see other Spheres with heavy techno-languages in them? Matter, Forces, Life. Forces may even be a better example, since to understand what Forces do, you have to know what is Kinetic Energy, Thermal Energy, Light, Sound and Electromagnetic (oh yes, and Gravity, almost forgot that one). Again, all of that, middle school science.<br /> <br /> For Matter, think about Matter 5... Change *density*... Basically everything Matter 5 does relates to some knowledge we earned in middle school science.<br /> <br /> And then, all of those get &quot;translated&quot; to a mystic paradigm. The player using Matter 5 to create a &quot;Sword of the Heavens&quot; will claim to the Master that he wants to &quot;bless his sword&quot; IN GAME, and OFF GAME he explains to the Master he's using Matter 5 to &quot;increase the density&quot; of the sword.<br /> <br /> A techno-boy explains to the Master that he's using &quot;Spirit (Dimensional Science) 4&quot; to &quot;trap the spirit (alien anomaly)&quot; in the ship's warp drive, and thus explains how he uses his &quot;quantum modulators&quot; to attune the anomaly wave-lenght to that of the drive, thus concluding the procedure.<br /> <br /> See? It's a common techno-hermetic background that gets translated into whatever babble the Mage's paradigm is.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a point here, but I would not concede that Mage: the Ascesion narration and detailed descriptions actually use Techomagical or Technocratic words, terms, or style in regard to theories or important explanations. I'd say that it is more likely - in most descriptions, at least - style and outlook of a Mage ot the Order of Hermes, or a Singer of the Celestial Choir, or a Verbenae. Though I admit it might be otherwise in some parts of M:tA writings, and I would be interested in some clear, direct indication that it is so in some of Mage books, preferebly in texts dealing with theories and ideas in regard to Magick Effects, or in writings relatively mundane and practical outlooks (relating to normal / mundane organizations or resource-related enterprises), or in descriptions of the Paradigms of various Mage groups (whether they would be Nephandi, Zantosa Revenant Mages, Taftani, Knight Templars, Ahi-i-Batini, or Technocrats). <br /> <br /> I would even say that the Tradition Mage - on whose style, attitude, and view points most descriptions in M:tA books are based - could very well be a Hermetic Mage who is a leader of a Tradition Chantry. Another option - perhaps some experienced travelling Chorister. Or maybe a Verbenae Witch who is responsible for the library and tutelage of other Tradition Mages in regard to various topics and areas of knowledge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}